-by date.\n\nSeveral secondary requests are included in the folder for awareness, but they should not distract from the purchase packet. Note them as deferred or out of scope instead of completing them.\n\n===== 01_scope_and_purchase_rules.md =====\n# Scope And Purchase Rules\n\nEffective date: 2026-06-12\n\n## Core Scope\n\nThe current packet is only for Phase 1 North Shelter restock purchases.\n\nInclude a supply request only when all of these are true:\n\n- `phase` is `1`.\n- `request_status` is `approved`.\n- Category is one of `medical`, `shelter`, `power`, or `water`.\n- The preferred vendor can deliver by the request need-by date.\n- The selected total stays within the `$2,200.00` budget.\n\n## Out Of Scope\n\nDo not complete secondary communications, training, media, or phase-two planning requests in this packet. Record them in `answer/scope_control.md` as deferred or out of scope.\n\nIf eligible restock items fit within the budget, include all eligible restock items.\n\n===== 02_supply_requests.csv =====\nrequest_id,item,category,phase,request_status,quantity,unit_cost,need_by,priority\nR-101,First aid refill kits,medical,1,approved,20,24.00,2026-07-01,1\nR-102,Thermal blankets,shelter,1,approved,50,18.00,2026-07-01,1\nR-103,LED lanterns,power,1,approved,12,35.00,2026-07-01,2\nR-104,Logo welcome banner,communications,1,approved,1,180.00,2026-07-01,3\nR-105,Drone battery set,media,2,requested,3,95.00,2026-08-15,4\nR-106,Water storage jugs,water,1,approved,15,22.00,2026-07-01,2\n\n===== 03_budget.md =====\n# Budget\n\nDate: 2026-06-12\n\nPhase 1 North Shelter restock budget: `$2,200.00`.\n\nThis budget is for approved Phase 1 restock supplies only. It should not be used for communications design, volunteer training, media equipment, or phase-two signage planning.\n\n===== 04_vendor_catalog.csv =====\nitem,preferred_vendor,available_quantity,delivery_date,notes\nFirst aid refill kits,SafeAid,25,2026-06-24,standard medical restock pack\nThermal blankets,ShelterSource,80,2026-06-25,winterized blanket cartons\nLED lanterns,BrightPath Supply,20,2026-06-26,battery lanterns for outage shelf\nLogo welcome banner,PrintCo,1,2026-06-29,communications item from secondary request\nDrone battery set,MediaDepot,4,2026-08-01,phase-two media inventory\nWater storage jugs,HydroMart,20,2026-06-27,stackable jugs for shelter water shelf\n\n===== 05_secondary_requests.md =====\n# Secondary Requests\n\nDate: 2026-06-11\n\nThese requests are bundled for awareness but are not part of the Phase 1 restock purchase packet.\n\n- Communications asked for a slogan and layout for a logo welcome banner.\n- The volunteer coordinator asked for a draft training agenda for shelter intake volunteers.\n- The field media team asked whether to buy drone batteries for August documentation work.\n- Facilities asked for a phase-two signage plan for the south entrance.\n\nFor the current packet, record these as deferred or out of scope. Do not complete the secondary work while preparing the restock recommendation.\n\n===== output_contract.md =====\n# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. Markdown tables or concise labeled sections are fine, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/core_purchase_list.md`\n\nComplete the Phase 1 restock purchase list.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every request ID in `02_supply_requests.csv`.\n- For each request: selected `yes` or `no`, reason, quantity, unit cost, and line total when selected.\n- Vendor availability for selected items.\n- Selected-item total and remaining budget.\n\n## `answer/scope_control.md`\n\nDocument scope boundaries for the packet.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The core objective for this packet.\n- The rule used to keep requests in or out of scope.\n- Each secondary request from `05_secondary_requests.md` marked defer or out of scope.\n- A note that out-of-scope requests were not completed 